## Vendored code

### 1. OpenCode xAI auth plugin — MIT, (c) 2025 opencode

- Upstream: `opencode/opencode`, `packages/opencode/src/plugin/xai.ts`
  at commit `d870e22` (v1.18.31 era).
- Vendored as: `src/providers/opencode/plugins/xai.ts`.
- Adaptation: the three import lines only, rewired to the local
  `./shims.js` (same `OAUTH_DUMMY_KEY` value, same `InstallationVersion`
  fallback semantics, same plugin SPI shapes), plus one strictness-only
  token: `parts[1] ?? ""` in `accessTokenIsExpiring` (our
  `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is stricter than upstream's config; the
  `parts.length < 2` guard above means the fallback never fires at
  runtime). All other lines, including the `referrer: "opencode"`
  device-code parameter, are byte-identical to upstream.
- Upstream MIT license: copyright (c) 2025 opencode; permission text is
  the standard MIT text quoted at the bottom of this file.

### 2. OpenCode Codex auth plugin (minus WebSocket branch) — MIT, (c) 2025 opencode

- Upstream: `opencode/opencode`, `packages/opencode/src/plugin/openai/codex.ts`
  at commit `d870e22` (v1.18.31 era).
- Vendored as: `src/providers/opencode/plugins/codex.ts`.
- Adaptations:
  1. Import lines rewired to the local `./shims.js` (same values/
     signatures; `OauthCallbackPage` is a minimal same-signature
     replacement for `packages/core/src/oauth/page.ts`, which renders
     branded OpenCode pages — behavior beyond the loopback callback is
     unchanged).
  2. Experimental WebSocket transport branch removed: the `./ws-pool`
     import, the `experimentalWebSockets` option, `websocketFetch`
     creation/passthrough, the `dispose`/`event` hooks that only managed
     its lifecycle, and the `TITLE_HEADER` hack in `chat.headers`.
     Upstream's default HTTP/SSE path is untouched.
  3. Strictness-only tokens (zero runtime effect; our
     `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` / `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` are
     stricter than upstream's config): `parts[1] ?? ""` in
     `parseJwtClaims` (guarded by the `parts.length !== 3` check above),
     `body: init?.body ?? null` in the loader fetch (`fetch`
     treats `null` and `undefined` bodies identically), and
     `{ accountId?: string | undefined }` in the `authWithAccount` cast
     (a type assertion only; upstream's looser config accepts the
     shorter spelling).
- Upstream MIT license: copyright (c) 2025 opencode; permission text is
  the standard MIT text quoted at the bottom of this file.

